{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21ec7e39d99b57bc5ac6", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Kinetic Theory of Gases - Test 1", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fded1"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde8c", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde25", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e08407faa0944a2c3d48da"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8edc"], "question": {"text": "If the collision frequency of hydrogen molecules in a closed chamber at $27^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ is $\\mathrm{Z}$, then the collision frequency of the same system at $127^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ is :"}, "options": [{"id": "45e28d", "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\mathrm{z}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde26"}, {"id": "017b64", "text": "$\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}} \\mathrm{Z}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde27"}, {"id": "355c72", "text": "$\\frac{3}{4} \\mathrm{Z}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde28"}, {"id": "b6000b", "text": "$\\frac{4}{3} \\mathrm{Z}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde29"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde2a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e08407faa0944a2c3d48df"], "concepts": ["6117b64d478ae845c43c682e"], "question": {"text": "The mean free path and the average speed of oxygen molecules at 300 K and 1 atm are $3 \\times 10^{-7} \\mathrm{~m}$ and $600 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$ respectively. Find the frequency of its collisions."}, "options": [{"id": "fe016b", "text": "$2 \\times 10^{10} / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde2b"}, {"id": "565f7c", "text": "$9 \\times 10^5 / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde2c"}, {"id": "e0d4e5", "text": "$2 \\times 10^9 / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde2d"}, {"id": "60acbe", "text": "$5 \\times 10^8 / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde2e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde2f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b6a"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87c9"], "question": {"text": "The internal energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>U</mi></mfenced></math>, pressure <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>P</mi></mfenced></math> and volume <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>V</mi></mfenced></math> of an ideal gas are related as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>P</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The gas is"}, "options": [{"id": "e49c4a", "text": "either monoatomic or diatomic", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde30"}, {"id": "e28a07", "text": "polyatomic only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde31"}, {"id": "d15fd2", "text": "monoatomic only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde32"}, {"id": "05c9e0", "text": "diatomic only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde33"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde34", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b87"], "concepts": ["60e567fa499d1e49588fa01f"], "question": {"text": "The temperature at which the kinetic energy of oxygen molecules becomes double than its value at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is"}, "options": [{"id": "b5bfd0", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>927</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde35"}, {"id": "92cd75", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>327</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde36"}, {"id": "6958b0", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1227</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde37"}, {"id": "784dd3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>627</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde38"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde39", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e08407faa0944a2c3d48da"], "concepts": ["6228bb8a5339ae4f881331fb"], "question": {"text": "A vessel contains <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of hydrogen and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>128</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of oxygen at standard temperature and pressure. The volume of the vessel in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> is :"}, "options": [{"id": "5e404d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>72</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde3a"}, {"id": "c01278", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>32</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde3b"}, {"id": "43292a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde3c"}, {"id": "0a35cd", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>54</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde3d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde3e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e08407faa0944a2c3d48df"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4705"], "question": {"text": "A <math><mn>25</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> volume cylinder is filled with <math><mn>1</mn></math> mol of <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> gas at room temperature <math><mo>(</mo><mn>300</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>)</mo></math> . The molecular diameter of <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> , and its root mean square speed, are found to be <math><mn>0.3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and <math><mn>200</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> , respectively. What is the average collision rate (per second) for an <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> molecule?"}, "options": [{"id": "cf991b", "text": "<math><mo>~</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>11</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde3f"}, {"id": "a32dd4", "text": "<math><mo>~</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde40"}, {"id": "658e86", "text": "<math><mo>~</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde41"}, {"id": "0a81a0", "text": "<math><mo>~</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>13</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde42"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde43", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b6a"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b566a"], "question": {"text": "Consider a mixture of <math><mi>n</mi></math> moles of helium gas and <math><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></math> moles of oxygen gas (molecules taken to be rigid) as an ideal gas. Its <math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math> value will be:"}, "options": [{"id": "f3b8ff", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>19</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>13</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde44"}, {"id": "d64fc7", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>67</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>45</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde45"}, {"id": "ad0c13", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>40</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>27</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde46"}, {"id": "525770", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>23</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde47"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde48", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b87"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b5a"], "question": {"text": "The number density of molecules of a gas depends on their distance r from the origin as, <math><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> Then the numer of molecules is proportional to:"}, "options": [{"id": "9aa144", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde49"}, {"id": "2135a7", "text": "<math><msqrt><msub><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><msup><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde4a"}, {"id": "3a681d", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde4b"}, {"id": "6cab79", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde4c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde4d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e08407faa0944a2c3d48df"], "concepts": ["6162fb096ed13040ec84a530"], "question": {"text": "At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>K</mi></math>, the rms speed of oxygen molecules is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mi>&#945;</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math>&nbsp;times to that of its average speed in the&nbsp;gas. Then, the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> will be (use&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>22</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math>)"}, "options": [{"id": "6c9991", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>32</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde4e"}, {"id": "e15250", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>28</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde4f"}, {"id": "a25aaa", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde50"}, {"id": "e4d089", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde51"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde52", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b6a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b2e"], "question": {"text": "Two moles of a monoatomic gas is mixed with six moles of a diatomic gas. The molar specific heat of the mixture at constant volume is :"}, "options": [{"id": "36335d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>R</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde53"}, {"id": "6dc059", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>R</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde54"}, {"id": "5a8570", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>R</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde55"}, {"id": "71658c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>R</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde56"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde57", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b87"], "concepts": ["6162fb086ed13040ec84a448"], "question": {"text": "What will be the average value of energy along one degree of freedom for an ideal gas in thermal equilibrium at a temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>?</mo></math> (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math> is Boltzmann constant)"}, "options": [{"id": "96352b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><mi>T</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde58"}, {"id": "a66feb", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><mi>T</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde59"}, {"id": "f0275a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><mi>T</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde5a"}, {"id": "b461f3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">B</mi></msub><mi>T</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde5b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde5c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e08407faa0944a2c3d48da"], "concepts": ["6176f4096581241c7072c435"], "question": {"text": "<p>A mixture of hydrogen and oxygen has volume <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2000</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>, pressure <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mi>kPa</mi></math> and mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>76</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>. The ratio of number of moles of hydrogen to number of moles of oxygen in the mixture will be</p><p>[Take gas constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>]</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "3511b1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde5d"}, {"id": "4ff500", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde5e"}, {"id": "43637f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde5f"}, {"id": "fe3c23", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/M