n>140</mn></math> ) have the same number density and are at the same temperature. The ratio of their respective mean free times is closest to:"}, "options": [{"id": "327f53", "text": "<math><mn>3.67</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde80"}, {"id": "5de987", "text": "<math><mn>1.83</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde81"}, {"id": "ac390d", "text": "<math><mn>2.3</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde82"}, {"id": "f62aa4", "text": "<math><mn>4.67</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde83"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde84", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b87"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b5a"], "question": {"text": "For an ideal gas the instantaneous change in pressure <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> with volume <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math> is given by the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>V</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> is the given boundary condition, then the maximum temperature one mole of gas can attain is:&nbsp;(Here <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is the gas constant)"}, "options": [{"id": "282291", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde85"}, {"id": "92203c", "text": "infinity", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde86"}, {"id": "811652", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde87"}, {"id": "61cef2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fde88"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:19.280Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:19.280Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdecf"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdecd", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdeb1", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e08407faa0944a2c3d48df"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4705"], "question": {"text": "The root-mean-square speed of molecules of a given mass of a gas at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> atmosphere pressure is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The root-mean-square speed of molecules of the gas at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>127</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> atmosphere pressure is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> will be __________."}, "options": [{"id": "89dfc8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdeb2"}, {"id": "b76c79", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdeb3"}, {"id": "c8f6e4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdeb4"}, {"id": "ade62e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdeb5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdeb6", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b87"], "concepts": ["6162fb086ed13040ec84a448"], "question": {"text": "A closed vessel contains <math><mrow><mn>0.1</mn></mrow></math> mole of a monoatomic ideal gas at <math><mrow><mn>200</mn><mtext>&#160;K</mtext></mrow></math>. If <math><mrow><mn>0.05</mn></mrow></math> mole of the same gas at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> is added to it, the final equilibrium temperature (in <math><mtext>K</mtext></math>) of the gas in the vessel will be close to ______"}, "options": [{"id": "3a09b5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdeb7"}, {"id": "87b3fc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdeb8"}, {"id": "8e6ed5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdeb9"}, {"id": "77c4a1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdeba"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdebb", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e08407faa0944a2c3d48da"], "concepts": ["60f34752eff4df09e43c25d3"], "question": {"text": "When a gas filled in a closed vessel is heated by raising the temperature by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>, its pressure increases by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>%</mo></math> The initial temperature of the gas is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "c39a60", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdebc"}, {"id": "e397d3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdebd"}, {"id": "5a220e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdebe"}, {"id": "a7ccaa", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdebf"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdec0", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b6a"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87c9"], "question": {"text": "$\\gamma_{\\mathrm{A}}$ is the specific heat ratio of monoatomic gas A having 3 translational degrees of freedom. $\\gamma_B$ is the specific heat ratio of polyatomic gas B having 3 translational, 3 rotational degrees of freedom and 1 vibrational mode. If $\\frac{\\gamma_{\\mathrm{A}}}{\\gamma_{\\mathrm{B}}}=\\left(1+\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}}\\right)$, then the value of $n$ is _______."}, "options": [{"id": "a07d23", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdec1"}, {"id": "d56687", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdec2"}, {"id": "cecfd7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdec3"}, {"id": "77a851", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdec4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdec5", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490c"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b6a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b2e"], "question": {"text": "One mole of a monoatomic gas is mixed with three moles of a diatomic gas. The molecular specific heat of mixture at constant volume is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>R</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>; then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> will be _____ . (Assume that the given diatomic gas has no vibrational mode.)"}, "options": [{"id": "8754fa", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdec6"}, {"id": "a7d98c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdec7"}, {"id": "8d4449", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdec8"}, {"id": "287460", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fdec9"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 5, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:19.366Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:19.366Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 1, "_id": "69de4f03c677dc36a88fded0"}], "bonusSections": [], "packDetails": [], "paidFeatures": [], "tags": [], "timeRestrictionSlots": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T11:15:56.782Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-17T04:57:59.298Z", "testType": "PYQs as Chapter Tests", "isResumeBufferAllowed": true, "enableAccessibility": true, "maxAttemptableQuestion": 25, "analysisVideoThumbnail": "", "analysisVideoThumbnailDark": "", "shortTitle": "", "subjectDetails": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73